  "description": "WESXEA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H132 Dy6 N2 O34. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.564-4.366 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.67-141.81°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(HL2)2(μ3-OH)2(μ3-OCH3)2(piv)10(MeOH)2] (C76H124Dy6N2O34). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
